Chromium 158.0.8127.36 -> 158.0.8127.88, for the 158.0.8127.36 tarball.

158.0.8127.88 is a tag on a minibranch of the 158 branch, 8127_36 (cut from
158.0.8127.36; refs/branch-heads/8127_36@{#32}), Google's Linux Stable release of 158
(2026-11-23) that has no source tarball (as of 2026-11-23: neither Google's lite
bucket nor chromium-linux-tarballs has it; the newest 158 tarball in both is .36).
The minibranch adds 32 commits to 158.0.8127.36, among them: the VariationsService
HTTP fallback off by default, hybrid post-quantum variations seed signatures with key
rotation, deserialization of older File System Access handles stored in IDB, Device
Sync's layered-studies denylist and X-Client-Data for WebView, and the VERSION
increments. No dependency's DEPS revision changes (DEPS is identical at both tags).

Generated from the upstream diff between the tags: chromium/src
refs/tags/158.0.8127.36..refs/tags/158.0.8127.88, as served by Gitiles, with
scripts/chromium-delta.

Left out, as they cannot affect a Linux build: files not in the release
tarball, iOS/Android/ChromeOS/Mac/Windows-only files, tests and docs,
translations (but en-GB), CI configuration, PGO/orderfile pointers, submodule
pointer updates, DEPS. GN files (*.gn, *.gni) are kept even for tests and other
platforms: gn gen reads test targets' BUILD.gn too.

Added: the tarball's stamp files for the new commit (stamps.py:
build/util/LASTCHANGE{,.committime}, gpu/config/gpu_lists_version.h and
build/util/MINIBRANCH, which becomes MINIBRANCH_BASE_VERSION=158.0.8127.36 on a
minibranch; commit 0cefb18236a23db1ebb6b2bc040fbbaf8cbe759e,
refs/branch-heads/8127_36@{#32}). skia/ext/skia_commit_hash.h,
gpu/webgpu/DAWN_VERSION and gpu/webgpu/dawn_commit_hash.h don't change.

Checked: applies to the 158.0.8127.36 tarball; chrome/VERSION becomes
158.0.8127.88; every patched source file is byte-identical to its version
at the tag; it adds and deletes no files; the 158.0.8127.36 tarball's non-git
files are all classified (tarball-generated.py with generated.conf).

Apply with git apply.

